<main class="main">
  <section class="legal-page">
    <h1><%= t("legal.terms_title") %></h1>

    <%#
      PASTE YOUR REAL TERMS BELOW.

      There are two sections further down - one for Czech (the "else"
      branch), one for German (the "if" branch). Replace the placeholder
      paragraph in each with your real text. Plain HTML works fine:
      headings, paragraphs, lists, bold text - the surrounding
      .legal-content CSS class already styles all of it, so no extra
      styling needed on your end.

      Until a German translation exists, just leave that section's
      placeholder as-is - it shows a short "coming soon" note instead.
    %>
    <div class="legal-content">
      <% if I18n.locale == :de %>
        <p><em><%= t("legal.terms_placeholder") %></em></p>
      <% else %>
        <p><em><%= t("legal.terms_placeholder") %></em></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
